1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,140
With her undeserved death, Asalem v. Seleucia, loyal subject and beloved member of the royal family, has revealed the truth to us.

2
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:17,260
Through her sacrifice, she has opened our eyes.

3
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:27,760
We seek justice. Earth has spat upon our good faith, heaped us with insult, and has committed this unspeakable atrocity.

4
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:34,900
And now, retribution is at hand because this day, we declare war against planet Earth!

5
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:48,680
Block 63B, clear! Block 63C, clear! There's no sign he's escaped from the castle! Track him down, now! Yes, sir!

6
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:55,200
Damn Terran. How could he use the audience chamber like that? I want him shot on sight!

7
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:58,900
Lord Cruteo, hold that thought a moment.

8
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:00,160
What is it, Lord Sosbo?

9
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:08,100
This boy is the son of Dr. Troyard. I believe we should question him more about his father's Alt-Noah research.

10
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:11,000
Could I trouble you to take him alive?

11
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,860
Continue. Tell me what happened after that.

12
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:21,880
And the orange cataphract. I need you to tell me more about it.

13
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:23,580
この悩南競陵 giveramination物か?

14
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:24,840
It does not come to me.

15
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:26,180
I need you to tell your story.

16
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:29,680
It is time for any invitation.

17
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:48,060
It is time for your future with goodoine.

18
00:01:48,060 --> 00:02:18,040
Thank you.

19
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:48,040
Thank you.

20
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:50,060
Thank you.

21
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:20,060
Thank you.

22
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:52,100
Attention, everyone! Assembly in the briefing room right now!

23
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,280
Hey, Yuki, what's going on?

24
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:56,260
Warrant Officer Kaisuka, please.

25
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,200
As of this moment, we're officially at war with them, too.

26
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:11,220
As of right now, you are all drafted into military service, subject to military regulations.

27
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:15,000
You are obligated to perform the duties of which you are assigned.

28
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,880
I look forward to seeing what you can do.

29
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,200
You're young. It's unfair.

30
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:25,460
But now you are warriors, and it's your job to safeguard the peace and safety of Earth.

31
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:33,020
This ship will resupply and put in for needed repairs at Tanigashima base.

32
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:37,400
Thereafter, we will likely go to UFE HQ in Russia.

33
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:41,460
All right, everyone. Please go to your assigned duty stations.

34
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:43,540
That is all. You are dismissed.

35
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:50,340
I'm Soma Yagarai, age 28. Specialties are surgery and behavioral medicine.

36
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,020
My door is always open if you ever need any counseling.

37
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:53,860
Thank you for your help, Doctor.

38
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:58,440
You see? My big sister has been too sick to go to school for a long time now.

39
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,660
Oh, is that so?

40
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:01,080
Isn't that right, Your Highness?

41
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:03,140
Uh, yes.

42
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:09,320
That's why Her Highness has never received any military training, because she's far too frail to be a soldier.

43
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:10,440
Oh.

44
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:14,440
However, as for myself, I can pilot a cataphract.

45
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:18,380
Well, when you're all grown up, please do, okay?

46
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:20,020
I will. Bye.

47
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:23,420
One more thing. Why do you call your sister Your Highness?

48
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:29,740
Because to me, my big sister is my beloved princess.

49
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:34,120
Please forgive my behavior, milady.

50
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,480
That's quite all right, and I thank you.

51
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:38,920
And what about you?

52
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,040
How old are you, please?

53
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:44,740
Everyone who had military training in high school is being drafted.

54
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:48,860
Well, I was kept out of school. For family reasons.

55
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:49,780
I see.

56
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:53,740
Well, there are plenty of things you can help with, even if you're not fighting.

57
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:58,400
You can still support everyone else who did get military training in school.

58
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:03,080
I'm sure you want to do your part to defend Earth against the Martians.

59
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:10,040
All right, McKay, we're clear.

60
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,360
Let's just back it up.

61
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:15,000
Why was I made a maintenance worker instead of a pilot?

62
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:17,660
You think it's because you flunked out of piloting?

63
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,880
Hey, mechanics are really crucial.

64
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:23,900
Without them, all the cataphracts would fall apart on us.

65
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:27,120
How am I supposed to waste any Martians stuck here in the hangar?

66
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:29,040
Hey, don't be so gung-ho.

67
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:34,080
These past 15 years, nobody's seen any real action out there.

68
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:36,680
Because all those who did are dead now.

69
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:38,460
That goes for the Martians, too.

70
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:42,920
Meaning that everybody, friend or foe, is a virgin to this, just like you.

71
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,040
Well, not everybody.

72
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:49,160
Inaho, you mean, are you saying that...

73
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,820
You lived through it, didn't you, Lieutenant?

74
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,760
And you're still alive.

75
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:55,060
Oh, that's what you're talking about.

76
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:57,300
Let's just say opinions are divided.

77
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:00,800
The Tanigashima report I wrote was buried really deep.

78
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,980
Tanigashima report is what?

79
00:07:03,980 --> 00:07:10,000
That's the place where the first fragments came to Earth when the moon was destroyed 15 years ago during Heaven's Fall.

80
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:11,060
Yeah.

81
00:07:12,260 --> 00:07:15,420
But something else came down well before the moon did.

82
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:18,600
Soldiers for the Empire.

83
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:25,760
We went up against those monstrous Martian cataphracts and dilapidated tanks that were obsolete.

84
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:28,000
They wiped us out.

85
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:33,400
Then the Hypergate went out of control and turned the moon into Heaven's Fall.

86
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:36,320
And the Martians wiped the battlefield clean.

87
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:41,040
But there's no physical evidence.

88
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:45,580
My report was deemed the ramblings of a madman written in terror.

89
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:46,880
But how could they?

90
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:47,940
It was the truth.

91
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:51,960
Mars' cataphracts are way beyond what Earth's technology can produce.

92
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:54,880
Either way, it'll be the same result.

93
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:58,240
Because Earth doesn't have Alt-Noah Drives.

94
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:00,960
Alt-Noah Drives.

95
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:08,180
Fugitive located.

96
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:09,840
He's in the Sky Carrier hangar.

97
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,560
Do not let him get away.

98
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:24,920
How long will he continue making me look like a fool?

99
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:31,320
The basics are the same as the training units.

100
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:40,180
Even with the higher output, if gravity and surface hardness don't change, agility will only decrease to the extent that its weight increases.

101
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:43,260
I'll just have to acclimate.

102
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,300
So this is where you've been?

103
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,280
All by yourself?

104
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:56,380
Yes.

105
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:00,080
This is beautiful.

106
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:01,480
Truly.

107
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:05,180
Is a blue sky that unusual to you?

108
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:06,100
Yes.

109
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,500
Are you studying something?

110
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,320
Just brushing up a little.

111
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,680
Don't know if it'll be very useful, though.

112
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:13,600
Oh, really?

113
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:14,240
Why not?

114
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:17,000
Because here on Earth, we don't have Alt-Noah.

115
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:17,800
Huh.

116
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:21,040
What is it anyway, Alt-Noah?

117
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:30,720
Alt-Noah is a kind of technology from a civilization that was discovered in ancient ruins on Verse.

118
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:33,440
Our world that you call Mars.

119
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:41,000
The first human to ever make contact and awaken it was Dr. Ray Regalia Verse Rayverse.

120
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:45,600
He is my grandfather and the Emperor of Verse.

121
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:59,980
And when it once again activated after so many eons, Alt-Noah saw Grandfather as its rightful heir, and branded his very genes with the Alt-Noah activation factor.

122
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:03,060
So then that means...

123
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:10,080
Yes, the only ones with the innate ability to use the power of Alt-Noah are Grandfather and his descendants.

124
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:20,160
In exchange for the knights swearing allegiance to him, he gave them the gift of Alt-Noah and its activation factor.

125
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:28,220
Using that power, the knights created mighty castles and cataphracts and ruled over the colonies.

126
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:38,140
Now, those who settled the desolate lands of Verse have turned jealous eyes on Earth.

127
00:10:38,820 --> 00:10:39,940
And its riches.

128
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:48,860
The cradle of all humanity, blessed with water and air in such abundance, that they refract light to make the sea and sky appear blue.

129
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:50,840
That's not accurate.

130
00:10:51,140 --> 00:10:51,500
Huh?

131
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:56,380
The blue sky isn't caused by diffraction. It's through the effects of Rayleigh scattering.

132
00:10:56,580 --> 00:11:00,060
What? But Slane said that it was caused by light diffraction.

133
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:05,040
The sky is blue from Rayleigh scattering, and the clouds are white from me scattering.

134
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:07,360
Your friend was mistaken.

135
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:09,960
Uh...

136
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,960
Hmm...

137
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:22,780
Excuse me. Would it be alright if I took over?

138
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,900
You're a real go-getter, aren't you?

139
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:27,360
I just want to get a feel for it.

140
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:28,640
What did you get in docking?

141
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:33,540
Oh, A-minus, sir. But still...

142
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:35,660
When we make port, stand next to me and watch.

143
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:37,400
And get your hands out of your sleeves.

144
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,160
Yes, sir. Sorry, sir. Thank you.

145
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:44,440
Aren't you guys supposed to give us some uniforms or something?

146
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:48,820
No, we haven't got enough right now. I'm hoping we can stock up on some at the next port.

147
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:54,620
That's not too hard on the eyes.

148
00:11:55,120 --> 00:12:00,100
Commander, why would we go to Tanegashima? I thought that area had been sealed off years ago.

149
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:05,980
With our lack of intel on their Mars landing castles, we want to stay away from likely invasion targets.

150
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:11,660
Tanegashima was devastated so badly that the very landscape was altered beyond recognition.

151
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:14,420
There's no longer a civilian population.

152
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,160
That makes sense.

153
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:19,840
So we're hoping the Martians in Tokyo won't choose it as a viable target.

154
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:33,500
I never thought I'd come back here.

155
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:40,580
Isn't it a little early for happy hour?

156
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:43,320
No, Doc. This drink isn't for me.

157
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:46,740
It's for the ones I'll never have the chance to again.

158
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:51,720
John Humoray? Is that who?

159
00:12:57,980 --> 00:12:58,580
Now this...

160
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:02,020
This one here is for me.

161
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:03,900
I'm jumping off the wagon.

162
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:05,640
You want a belt, Doc?

163
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:07,960
Yeah, maybe I will.

164
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,540
Mind if I join you?

165
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:12,540
Captain Magburetch.

166
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:18,860
The Tanegashima report.

167
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:22,580
I've heard rumors about it, of course.

168
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:26,280
But I never once believed that it was a fabrication.

169
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:29,780
And that, Lieutenant Marito...

170
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:33,540
Is why I have not been able to forgive you.

171
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:39,180
That battle on Tanegashima...

172
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:41,560
My big brother fought in it, too.

173
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:44,440
He was killed in action.

174
00:13:46,180 --> 00:13:47,040
Murdered, rather.

175
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:48,480
By you.

176
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:53,200
Magburetch is the name of the family who adopted me.

177
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:55,600
My birth name was Humoray.

178
00:13:57,760 --> 00:14:00,420
Your best friend was my only brother, John.

179
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:14,300
What's that?

180
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,840
All anti-air units, get out to sea!

181
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:27,880
Hard right-runner! Combat speed!

182
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,460
Huh? Me, ma'am?

183
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:31,620
Give me a damage report.

184
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,920
Missile impact midship. No detonation.

185
00:14:34,220 --> 00:14:36,700
Appears to be a dud. But be careful down there.

186
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:39,080
What is it?

187
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:43,020
It's moving. It's alive.

188
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,100
What the hell was that? I need intel.

189
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,100
It's coming back.

190
00:14:57,880 --> 00:15:02,900
Help is not answering. It's going to hit.

191
00:15:03,060 --> 00:15:04,900
All hands. Brace for impact now.

192
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:09,900
Let's go.

193
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:24,900
Entering my territory without so much as a by-your-leave?

194
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:39,560
Oh, this just will not do.

195
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:42,000
I fear a lesson is needed.

196
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:44,540
A very harsh one indeed.

197
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:48,200
What is it doing this far out?

198
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:51,080
I think this is a different Martian than the one in Tokyo.

199
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,300
Shipboard cataphrats, prepare to launch.

200
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:55,580
Freezing platoon, launch.

201
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,500
Elevator one, engaged.

202
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:02,140
Calm. Huh?

203
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:03,940
It's not powering up.

204
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:06,240
Sorry. We're running a systems check.

205
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:07,640
Just give us a minute.

206
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:17,500
It feels kind of cramped in here.

207
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:20,000
You know?

208
00:16:22,380 --> 00:16:25,300
Okay. Force feedback checking program starting.

209
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:27,020
Ejection seat functional.

210
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:28,480
IFF online.

211
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:30,820
Tactical data link is activated.

212
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:32,360
All systems green.

213
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:40,940
Mustang leader to Mustang 2-2.

214
00:16:41,180 --> 00:16:43,820
Now, you're in a training unit, so you'll be our marksman.

215
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:44,700
Is that you, Yuki?

216
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:45,980
But your arm is still...

217
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:47,280
If my newbie's in the fight,

218
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:49,260
don't really see how I can sit this one out.

219
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,580
But warrant Officer Kaizuka.

220
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:52,100
Yuki will be just fine.

221
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,480
Mustang leader, out.

222
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:58,680
Unbelievable.

223
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:05,640
Mustang leader, Yuki Kaizuka, commencing launch.

224
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:08,760
Raising elevator number two, and vehicle elevator.

225
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:11,140
Frisian platoon, you're on the bow position.

226
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:13,500
Mustang platoon, deploy to the stern.

227
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:16,220
All units, intercept airborne enemies.

228
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,000
I almost feel sorry.

229
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:25,120
Poor inferior race trying to get by without Alt-Noah.

230
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:28,040
Cower before my might.

231
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:29,680
Bow down before me.

232
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:31,600
Then despair and die.

233
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:37,740
Now fly, my mighty messengers.

234
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:54,080
Eye unit, you're too close together.

235
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:54,720
Spread out.

236
00:17:58,040 --> 00:18:01,300
They are tough.

237
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,640
My fists become a giant molecule.

238
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:05,720
Your bullets can't do a thing.

239
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:07,560
Mustang leader to all units.

240
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:09,120
AP rounds are ineffective.

241
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:12,100
All units switch to high explosives and attack.

242
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:12,580
Right.

243
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:13,000
Roger.

244
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:13,300
Roger.

245
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:15,080
Ah, crap.

246
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:17,900
Lieutenant Marito, where are you going?

247
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:19,680
I'm playing my home field again.

248
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:21,960
I am on a team, right?

249
00:18:27,140 --> 00:18:30,380
Or maybe this is an away game.

250
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:39,980
Hey, Yinko, watch her backs.

251
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:40,980
Roger that.

252
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:52,240
Get on your feet.

253
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:53,240
You're a sitting duck.

254
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:54,340
Oh, right.

255
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:55,920
Inaho, I'm sorry.

256
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:56,900
